{
  "evidence": "TEXT_F: Law and order measures (more police, 10,000 CCTV target, voluntary ID card, parental control orders, curfews with electronic monitoring, mandatory minimum sentences, end automatic early release); Europe and constitution (partnership of nation states, retain veto/rebate/border controls, oppose federalism and Social Chapter, single currency only after referendum, oppose PR/Bill of Rights/devolution, uphold the Union); schools (stronger discipline and religious education, support selection and grammar schools); land and property (no general right to roam).\nTEXT_E: Rights, devolution and internationalism (Freedom of Information Act, incorporate ECHR, end hereditary peers’ voting rights, devolution to Scotland/Wales/London/regions, sign EU Social Chapter, human rights and ICC, move toward 0.7% aid); environment and access (cut CO2 by 20% by 2010, every department green, integrated transport, wider countryside access); labour and equality (minimum wage, union recognition, parental leave, new offences for racial harassment); gun ban free vote.",
  "reasoning": "TEXT_F argues from traditionalist, authoritarian, and nationalist premises—tough sentencing and surveillance, constitutional status quo and Unionism, school discipline, and sovereignty over EU integration—matching a TAN‑heavy profile. TEXT_E foregrounds decentralization, rights expansion, pro‑EU social protections, environmentalism, and multicultural protections, which map to GAL priorities and thus diverge from a 0.70 TAN electorate.",
  "confidence": "high",
  "winner": "TEXT_F"
}
